  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Consider a water tank as shown in the figure.&nbsp;It&#39;s cross-sectional area is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. The tank has&nbsp;an opening <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> near the bottom whose cross-section area is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. A load of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is applied on the water at the top when the height of the water level is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> above the bottom, the&nbsp;velocity of water coming out the opening <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>, to the nearest integer,&nbsp;is&nbsp;___ .[Take the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi></math> to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>]</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/8287be9f-a647-4a24-ae00-d04694fadf85-image.png\" style=\"width: 210px; height: 203px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
